        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(localization): consolidate product surfaces",
        "body": "RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/42\r\n\r\nRelated: #88570, #81253, #79458, #55239, #89971, #78038\r\n\r\nFoundation series: 4 of 5.\r\nReview order: #111541 -> #111542 -> #111543 -> #111544 -> #111545.\r\nOriginal slices: giodl73-repo/openclaw#125, giodl73-repo/openclaw#126, giodl73-repo/openclaw#128, and giodl73-repo/openclaw#130.\r\n\r\nThis draft targets `main`, so its GitHub diff is cumulative until foundation PRs 1-3 land. Its intended review boundary is signed commits `e6049705441` and `46cff72dd02`.\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nCLI, TUI, Gateway, channel safety, command, skill, and plugin presentation still contain product-owned hardcoded copy or inconsistent localization boundaries. Users can select a locale in one client but still see English approval prompts, Gateway failures, slash-command descriptions, Telegram menus, or skill metadata.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nThis applies the shared contract to remaining CLI/TUI presentation, Gateway error descriptors and Control UI rendering, channel approval safety copy, and localized command, skill, and plugin metadata without changing stable machine identities.\r\n\r\n## Main Interface And Design\r\n\r\nThe shared presentation-metadata interface is:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ntype LocalizedText = {\r\n  default: string;\r\n  localizations?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\r\n};\r\n\r\nnormalizeLocalizedText(input, options?): LocalizedTextNormalizationResult;\r\nresolveLocalizedText(metadata, locale, scope?): string;\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor product-owned metadata, locale keys must resolve through the OpenClaw registry. External plugin metadata may use canonicalizable BCP 47 tags. Normalization rejects conflicting legacy/object maps, invalid or duplicate locales, display controls, oversized maps, and invalid translations.\r\n\r\nThe Gateway command wire contract adds one optional field without changing command identity:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ntype CommandEntry = {\r\n  name: string;\r\n  description: string;\r\n  descriptionLocalizations?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\r\n  // existing source, scope, arguments, aliases...\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nSkill frontmatter normalizes into `OpenClawSkillMetadata.presentation.displayName` and `.description`. Gateway, Control UI, CLI, TUI, Telegram, and Discord resolve or project the same normalized metadata. TUI rendering is similarly bounded by `TuiLocalization { context, t }`.\r\n\r\nChannel approvals use `ApprovalMessageRenderer` and typed action descriptors at the final delivery boundary. Command names, skill/plugin IDs, protocol values, authorization decisions, and approval payloads remain stable; only presentation fields vary. Safety copy falls back as one whole English message family when recipient locale ownership or review evidence is missing.\r\n\r\nGateway error descriptor identities come from\r\n`packages/gateway-protocol`; server projection and Control UI rendering use the\r\nsame protocol-owned registry while retaining surface-owned catalogs. The\r\ncoverage report likewise consumes the product-surface declarations published\r\nby the relevant owner/domain modules rather than a closed list in localization\r\ncore.\r\n\r\n## Example\r\n\r\nThe command remains `/status` everywhere, but its description may project as localized metadata:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"name\": \"status\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Show current OpenClaw status\",\r\n  \"descriptionLocalizations\": {\r\n    \"de\": \"Aktuellen OpenClaw-Status anzeigen\",\r\n    \"ja\": \"現在の OpenClaw ステータスを表示\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nTelegram, Discord, Control UI, CLI, and TUI can consume the same presentation identity without translating `/status`. Likewise, an approval message localizes labels and guidance while preserving the exact command, host, request ID, and approve/deny semantics.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nUsers receive locale-aware presentation across major operator and channel surfaces, with explicit English fallback behavior for safety-critical messages.\r\n\r\n## Final Exact-Head Proof\r\n\r\nAt `46cff72dd02ae489ca29f8a5490225376c291d78`, the focused Gateway,\r\nControl UI, approval, metadata, TUI, and Telegram contract set passes 269 tests\r\nacross 22 files. The branch contains no localization release claim in\r\n`CHANGELOG.md`.\r\n\r\nThe existing [Mantis Telegram Desktop proof](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/111544#issuecomment-5017549766)\r\nshows the candidate behavior at `e6049705441`. The follow-up to the current\r\nhead changes only changelog cleanup, shared Gateway descriptor plumbing, and\r\ncoverage ownership; it does not change the Telegram-visible implementation.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\nThe intended PR 4 change is the verified Gio-signed product-surface commit\r\n`e6049705441`; follow-up `46cff72dd02` carries the shared Gateway protocol\r\nboundary and owner-published coverage declarations through this cumulative\r\nbranch.\r\n",
